 61NI    59CO(7LI,ANG):XUNDL-5         2019Sa04                           201905
 61NI c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2019Sa04: Phys Rev C 99, 014315    
 61NI2c  (2019)                                                                 
 61NI c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), January 24, 2019                      
 61NI c  2019Sa04: E=22-24 MeV {+7}Li beam was produced from the Pelletron      
 61NI2c  LINAC Facility at the Tata Institute of Fundamental Research (TIFR),   
 61NI3c  Mumbai. Target was 5.2 mg/cm{+2} mono-isotopic {+59}Co on a 4          
 61NI4c  mg/cm{+2} Ta foil. |g rays were detected with the an array of 11       
 61NI5c  Compton-suppressed Clover detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,     
 61NI6c  |g|g|g-coin, |g|g(ADO), |g|g(DCO), |g(lin pol). Deduced levels, J,     
 61NI7c  |p, |g-ray multipolarities, branching ratios. Comparisons with         
 61NI8c  shell-model calculations.                                              
 61NI cG $DCO ratios are given under comments with DCO(D) for gate on a pure    
 61NI2cG dipole transition and DCO(Q) on a pure quadrupole. Expected DCO        
 61NI3cG ratios are 0.59 {I1} for a pure dipole and 0.95 {I1} for a pure        
 61NI4cG quadrupole when gating on a pure quadrupole transition; the values     
 61NI5cG are 0.96 {I2} and 1.74 {I1}, respectively, when gating on a pure       
 61NI6cG dipole transition (2019Sa04)                                           
 61NI cG $Expected ADO ratios are 1.24 {I2} for pure quadurpole transitions     
 61NI2cG and 0.81 {I2} for pure dipole transitions (2019Sa04).                  
 61NI cG $For polarization values given under comments, positive values         
 61NI2cG indicate electric nature of the transitions and negative values        
 61NI3cG indicate magnetic nature (2019Sa04).                                   
 61NI cG E(X)$Newly identified transitions by 2019Sa04                          
 61NI cG M$From 2019Sa04 based on measured |g|g(DCO), |g|g(ADO) and  |g(lin     
 61NI2cG pol) data, given under comments.                                       
 61NI cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies (by compiler)            
 61NI cL E(Y)$New levels proposed by 2019Sa04                                   
 61NI cL J$As given in 2019Sa04, based on measured |g|g(DCO), |g|g(ADO) and     
 61NI2cL |g(lin pol), and known assignments for low-lying states.               
 61NI cL J(A)$Taken by 2019Sa04 from Adopted Levels of {+61}Ni in ENSDF         
 61NI2cL database                                                               
